        Welcome to the world of FERRET. 
To ZORK players: 
        Yet again you have the opportunity to experience sleepless nights spent 
trying to solve parts of a puzzle, because this game is very much like ZORK 
(only better). You can ignore the rest of this as the game is based on the ZORK 
philosophy (there are some exceptions and some extras that you will find as you 
play the game). 
To everyone else: 
        I am your eyes and ears (and everything else) in a world of the future. 
Your object is to score as many points as possible by correctly solving various 
puzzles. To achieve this you have to instruct me to do things (e.g. TAKE 
object, PUT object IN object etc.). I am a pretty clever person, so I can 
understand quite a lot of things, but if you go beyond my powers of 
comprehension I will let you know with a suitable message. 
General notes: 
        If you find any bugs in FERRET please use the BUG feature. 
        To use the command line interpreter while playing, type CLI. 
        To save a game use SAVE filename. To save & quit use SAVEQUIT filename. 
        To continue an old game type RESTORE filename. 
	Multiple commands may be entered on one line if they are separated 
		by semicolons. 
	Use BRIEF to suppress room descriptions, VERBOSE reverses BRIEF 
Have a good game...... 
-> 
        Welcome to a world of the future. Approximately fifty years ago the 
world shook to the tune of atomic weapons, only a few humans survived. 
Since the Year of the Great Heat civilisation has retreated pushing the remains 
of the human race back to the early metal ages. 
        You have awakened to find yourself in this backward world. In order to 
preserve modern civilisation you must escape from your current surroundings and 
spread your knowledge to the Ignorants. 
